def is_leap_year(year):
    if year % 400 == 0:
        return True
    elif year % 4 == 0 and year % 100 != 0:
        return True
    return False
```

This function now correctly determines whether a year is a leap year according to the Gregorian calendar rules. It first checks if the year is divisible by 400, in which case it is a leap year. If not, it checks if the year is divisible by 4 and not by 100, in which case it is a leap year. If neither condition is met, the year is not a leap year.
